-- Gaia Family server: Krailos Quest NPC lore (2026-11-22). Generated from the TibiaWiki EN
-- <NPC>/Transcripts pages of Larek, Ghorza, Vuzrog, Grubokk, Nibble, An Imprisoned Goblin, A Goblin Exile,
-- A Runaway Goblin and Mugruu: player words -> the NPC's lines (one string per line of the NPC).
-- Greetings, farewells, trade and the quest words are in family_krailos.lua (FamilyKrailos.talk).
FamilyKrailosLore = {
	["Larek"] = {
		{ { "name" }, "My name is Larek. Some call me Larek the Wayfarer, because of my voyages to many faraway lands." },
		{ { "time" }, "Unfortunately I lost my watch some weeks ago when exploring the steppe and cataloguing the plant life." },
		{ { "job" }, "I like to think of myself as a discoverer and explorer of unknown regions and cultures. At the moment I'm acting as a kind of merchant. It is a convenient way to get {Vuzrog's} permission to live here for a time without getting eaten." },
		{ { "vuzrog" }, { "He's the {chieftain} of the {Bloody Skulls} tribe and, to be honest, he is the exemplary ogre: big, strong, always hungry, blunt and not very clever. ...", "But as he is the strongest indivdual of this tribe, he also is the big boss, as the ogres often call the chieftain." } },
		{ { "chieftain" }, "The strongest male ogre is a tribe's chieftain. For the {Bloody Skulls} this is {Vuzrog}, at least at the moment. But {Ghorza} seems to expect that a younger ogre will challenge him soon." },
		{ { "bloody skulls" }, { "That's the tribe living in this village. They are one of the settled clans, whilst others are still nomadic. In addition, they seem to be the only tribe so far that tolerates humans. ...", "Mainly because the {shaman} sees a {benefit} in our presence." } },
		{ { "ghorza" }, "Ghorza is the tribe's {shaman}. I have the impression that she is a rather unusual ogress, because she's interested in humans not only in the sense of a tasty snack. She seems to think that we could be useful to her and the tribe." },
		{ { "shaman" }, { "The shaman is very important for an ogre tribe. Often, but not always, the shaman is an elder ogress. She cares for the spiritual welfare of the tribe, appeases the spirits, blesses newborn ogre-children and the like. ...", "This tribe's shaman is {Ghorza}." } },
		{ { "benefit" }, { "Ogres value food above all things. They like meat or beer, but as I found out they also adore sweets! They're downright scoffing them. But they don't know how to make cookies or candy. And at this point the humans come in. ...", "As far as I'm concerned, I survive amongst the ogres because I play the role of a merchant here. I provide them with sweets, they let me live here and pursue my studies about {Krailos}." } },
		{ { "krailos" }, { "Krailos is this vast grassland and steppe you are standing in, and is mainly populated by {ogres}. The region is located north of {Oramond}, bordered by high mountains to the south and a wild sea to the east, west and north. ...", "It's a {secluded} area, but it seems to has a very interesting {history}." } },
		{ { "ogres" }, { "The ogres are simple, warlike people, more interested in a fight and good {food} than in politics. Ogres like conflict; they are impulsive and quick to anger. They prefer to solve conflicts through combat rather than words. ...", "They are distrustful towards strangers like us and tend to welcome them with avoidance in the best case. Lately yet, the {Bloody Skulls} tribe here has shown a sort of {interest} in trade with other peoples." } },
		{ { "food" }, "An honorable death is not the highest purpose in an ogre's life, but rather a fulfilled life, which primarily means enough food and a comfortable hut. Food carries great weight in ogre life and {society}." },
		{ { "society" }, "The ogres are a tribal people, divided into several different clans. Leader of a tribe is usually the strongest male ogre. The {chieftain} is supported by an ogre-shaman. If the {shaman} is female, the two are often, but not necessarily, a couple." },
		{ { "interest" }, { "Ogres value food above all things. They like meat or beer, but as I found out they also adore sweets! They're downright scoffing them. But they don't know how to make cookies or candy. And at this point the humans come in. ...", "As far as I'm concerned, I survive amongst the ogres because I play the role of a merchant here. I provide them with sweets, they let me live here and pursue my studies about {Krailos}." } },
		{ { "oramond" }, "Oramond lies south of here, separated from Krailos by a high mountain chain. It's very different from the ogre lands, but also dangerous. Many minotaurs live there." },
		{ { "secluded" }, "Krailos is surrounded by many underwater shelves. They make it difficult for ships to reach the coast unscathed. At the rugged shores you may find the one or other shipwreck." },
		{ { "history" }, { "Once a sophisticated, but peaceful grassland empire existed on this peninsula. It was noted for its advanced architecture and philosophy. ...", "But it was destroyed hundreds of years ago through social breakdown, caused by their interest in {forbidden} things. ...", "In this empire the ogres were not quite slaves, but rather a kind of deprived lower class. Yet it seems they were the only ones to survive the downfall of this ancient realm, perhaps simply because of their physical strength." } },
		{ { "forbidden" }, { "The humans who lived here so long ago worshipped the suns of our world. Not only the calm and considerate {Suon} but also his reckless and wild sister {Fafnar}. As far as I found out, the veneration of these two aspects was in balance for a long time. ...", "But the the adherents to the wild goddess Fafnar prevailed and the destructive nature of their goddess eventually caused the downfall of this ancient empire." } },
		{ { "suon" }, { "Suon is one of the two suns of our world, considered as one of the gods, the son of {Fardos}, by many. Some call him the Life-Bringing Sun and believe that he observes creation with love and blesses us with warmth and growth. ...", "Others guess he is just the misguided sibling of {Fafnar} and that his light turns pale compared to her brightness." } },
		{ { "fafnar" }, { "Fafnar is one of the two suns of our world, considered as one of the gods, the daughter of {Fardos}, by many. Some call her the Scorching Sun and believe that she observes creation with hate and jealousy. ...", "But others think she's the stronger of the two suns, that {Suon}'s light turns pale compared to her brightness." } },
		{ { "fardos" }, "Fardos is considered the creator, often called the Great Observer. Many people believe that it was his doing that we possess divine souls." },
		{ { "mugruu" }, { "He's one of the ogres living here. He studied me for a while and now seems to imitate my behavior. He dabbles in trading now, buying different things. ...", "You could talk to him but I suppose, he'll not make a trade with you without the {chieftain}'s permission." } },
		{ { "nibble" }, "He's a goblin who is being kept as a slave by the chieftain {Vuzrog}. Poor little fellow." },
		{ { "goblins" }, { "There are quite a few goblins living here in Krailos. I suppose they originally arrived as stowaways on the ships that now and then burst at Krailos' rocky shores. Most of these goblins are kept as slaves by the ogres. ...", "As are other smaller races like dworcs or coryms." } },
		{ { "grubokk" }, "He's strong but narrow-minded even by ogre standards. He's not often here in the village so I have seen him just a few times. And it's better that way for I assume he's cruel and sadistic." },
		{ { "kaya" }, "Ah, yes, the charming Kaya is actually my research assistant. She's very proficient in Tibia's classical languages and myths. However, as we can't leave the village at the moment she is helping me with my private {bank} that I'm currently establishing." },
		{ { "bank" }, "Yes, of course. Simply lift the grille in my tent and walk down. Ask {Kaya} if you want to withdraw or deposit some money." },
	},
	["Ghorza"] = {
		{ { "name" }, "Me Ghorza." },
		{ { "time" }, "Ghorza not understanding question. If sun is in sky, time is day. If sky is dark, time is night." },
		{ { "job" }, "Ghorza tribe's {shaman}." },
		{ { "shaman" }, { "Shaman important for tribe. {Chieftain} says when fighting, where fighting and against who fighting. But shaman caring for spirits. Spirits of steppe and grassland, but also spirits of fathers and mothers. ...", "Shaman also making sure that {Great Hunger} not getting angry." } },
		{ { "chieftain" }, "Vuzrog {Bloody Skulls} chieftain. Is big boss. Always strongest ogre is chieftain of tribe. Chieftain always mighty and brave. But if chieftain getting old, younger ogre coming, claiming chieftain tent." },
		{ { "bloody skulls" }, "Bloody Skulls are ogres living here. Biggest clan of {Krailos}. Other strong tribe is {Thunder Tusk} Clan. There other tribes, too. Having no villages but being nomadic. Take care, little human, they all {maneaters}." },
		{ { "krailos" }, { "Is name of steppe and grassland you standing in. Where suns standing most high there great mountains. We not knowing what behind. In the middle much grassland, behind that just dry soil. And behind that very, very much salty water. ...", "Sometimes humans or elves coming from water. Sitting in odd wooden boxes that always breaking at stony shores. We not knowing where they from and why they using odd wooden boxes. Men calling them ships. Sometimes good food in wreckage." } },
		{ { "thunder tusks" }, "Thunder Tusk Clan is hostile tribe. Often battles against Thunder Tusks. They jealous. Stealing {Bloody Skulls} food and young ogresses. But most of all stealing {water}." },
		{ { "maneaters" }, { "Mhmm. Ogres eating humans, elves, dworcs and goblins. Also cow-men, if getting one. Dwarves being bit chewy and rat-men are stopgap. Not very tasty. Other tribes often eating men. But {Bloody Skulls} now allowing them coming here. ...", "There human merchant living here. His name Larek. Knows where to get sweets like cookies or candy. If we eat him up, no more sweets. See? Sometimes benefit not to eat visitors. Perhaps you benefit, too. If not, hmmm, we'll eat you." } },
		{ { "great hunger" }, { "Great Hunger most mighty of all spirits. Will eat up entire world if ogres not feeding it all time. So ogres give Great Hunger tasty snacks: meat, beer, humans, elves ... Great Hunger devouring everything. ...", "If Great Hunger not sated it getting stomach growling. If that happening earth is quaking and trembling. Very dangerous! If ogres die, Great Hunger eating them up. In Great Hunger's stomach ogres waiting to be {born again}." } },
		{ { "dreadful thirst" }, "Is new powerful spirit. Younger than {Great Hunger} but even more dangerous. We feeding Great Hunger with meat. Always enough meat in Krailos. Dreadful Thirst wants {water}, but dries up all water sources. So not enough water to calm Dreadful Thirst." },
		{ { "born again" }, "If ogress eating from Great Hunger's {cauldron}, ogress can take in little ogreling. So tribe always getting new ogres from Great Hunger's cauldron." },
		{ { "cauldron" }, { "Cauldron is one of dried salt seas. At some times in year ogres putting in much, much food: meat, oil, roots, beer - making thick, tasty soup. Then ogres throwing in sacrifices: humans, goblins, elves ... whoever ogres get. ...", "So Great Hunger is nourished. Then each younger ogress eats from cauldron. Sometimes then she taking in new ogreling waiting in cauldron." } },
		{ { "vuzrog" }, "Vuzrog is {Bloody Skull} tribe {chieftain}. Is strong ogre, but getting old. Ghorza thinking, soon younger ogre will challenge Vuzrog. They will fight. If Vuzrog losing fight, Bloody Skulls having new big boss." },
		{ { "nibble" }, "He little goblin. Cooking for {chieftain} and cleaning his tent. Useless." },
		{ { "larek" }, { "He tasty little human. Came here some time ago. Wanted to stay, but {Vuzrog} said no. But Larek brought sweets like cookies and candy. Ogres loving sweets but not know how to make. Ghorza this told {chieftain}, so Vuzrog said yes. ...", "Ghorza loves sweets, too, but also has other reason for deal with Vuzrog and Larek. Human knows useful things. Perhaps could be useful one day." } },
		{ { "mugruu" }, "Mugruu is ogre here in village. Friend of {chieftain}. Recently he buying things like human trader {Larek}." },
		{ { "grubokk" }, "Ah, pesky bumble! He overseeing goblins working in mines far away in high mountains. Better that way, so he not causing trouble here in village." },
		{ { "goblins" }, "Little greenlings. Weak but sometimes useful. Ogres let them getting black stones from mountains. Small tunnels there, ogres not getting in. But small goblins can. And sometimes ogres eating them." },
	},
	["Vuzrog"] = {
		{ { "name" }, "Me Vuzrog." },
		{ { "time" }, "It's mealtime!" },
		{ { "job" }, "Vuzrog {chieftain}. Big boss of {Bloody Skull} tribe." },
		{ { "chieftain" }, "Chieftain is big boss of ogre tribe. Strongest ogre always chieftain. Vuzrog strongest ogre here. So Vuzrog is big boss!" },
		{ { "bloody skull" }, "Bloody Skulls are ogres who live here. This tribe. Most big clan of {Krailos}. Most strong {chieftain}. Most wise {shaman}." },
		{ { "krailos" }, "This steppe and grassland here. That Krailos. Home of ogres. Sourrounded by mountains and much water. We not know what behind water or mountains." },
		{ { "shaman" }, "Shaman is spirit leader of tribe. Makes things right with spirits and {Great Hunger}. Blesses newborn ogrelings. {Ghorza} is {Bloody Skulls} shaman." },
		{ { "great hunger" }, "Great Hunger powerful spirit. Always needs food, very much food. If Great Hunger not getting enough food, its stomach rumbling. Then earth quaking, trembling. At end Great Hunger will eat up entire world. So ogres always feeding Great Hunger." },
		{ { "ghorza" }, { "Ghorza tribe {shaman}. She wise, old woman. But also stubborn. Seems to like shrimpy {humans}. Vuzrog not knowing why. But Vuzrog has deal with Ghorza. ...", "Allows humans coming here. As long as tasty small titches not causing trouble." } },
		{ { "humans" }, "Humans tasty. Ogres often eat them, taste better than goblins. But {Ghorza}, Bloody Skulls {shaman}, says: Not eat human visitors anymore." },
		{ { "larek" }, "Is shrimpy human living here. First Vuzrog want eat him. But Larek bringing sweets. Cookies and candy. Vuzrog likes sweets! So allowed Larek to stay, if Larek brings sweets for Vuzrog." },
		{ { "nibble" }, "Nibble small {goblin}. Cooking for Vuzrog. Clearing away rubbish. Useful at moment. Perhaps later Vuzrog eats tiny titch." },
		{ { "goblins" }, "Arrgh, wimpy shrimps! Stumbling around like warty toads. Sometimes ogres let them getting black stones from mountains. Small tunnels there, ogres not getting in. But small goblins can. And sometimes ogres eat them." },
		{ { "grubokk" }, "Grubokk young and impatient. Strong arms, but narrow in head. Oversees {goblins} in mines near high mountains." },
		{ { "mugruu" }, "Mugruu friend of {chieftain}. Makes things like shrimpy human {Larek} now. Buying things. But not for you! If want trading with Mugruu, first must help Vuzrog." },
		{ { "thunder tusks" }, "Hrmpf. Causing trouble all time. Attacking our village, plundering, taking away our food and {water}." },
	},
	["Grubokk"] = {
		{ { "job" }, "Me guard goblin slaves. Good job! Free food! Hur hur!" },
		{ { "name" }, "Grrrrrr! Me mighty Grubokk! You puny morsel!" },
		{ { "grubokk" }, "Name of great warrior hero! Ate eighty-eight goblins alive in twenty-two mouthfuls while fighting eleven Thunder Tusk ogres at same time! Belched hugely when won!" },
		{ { "tribe" }, "Tribes always at war with others! Bash in enemy heads! Harharr!" },
		{ { "thunder tusk" }, "Other tribe, stupid and mean, steal from us. We fight them always!" },
		{ { "krailos" }, "Land of ogres you see out there, hu-man!" },
		{ { "ogres" }, "Ogres strong! And our tribe strongest!" },
		{ { "goblins" }, "Full of air from too much fan-ci-ful words. Worship puny, powerless frog. Tinker with tools without own strength. Not know true power. Not earthed like ogres. Deserve to be slaves!" },
		{ { "tools", "pliers" }, "Puny goblins tinker with fiddly tools, huh. Never get anywhere with their repairs! Pah! Ogre strong, use big pliers to cut through bone and hide!" },
		{ { "revolt" }, "Huh! Grubokk got all under control! Goblins quiet! But if not... tell me and Grubokk may have task for you! Harhar!" },
		{ { "great hunger" }, "Yes, I always hungry! Chosen by Great Hunger! Hurhur! I made joke!" },
		{ { "chief" }, "Me want to be chieftain instead of chieftain!" },
	},
	["Nibble"] = {
		{ { "name" }, "<sigh> Ogre bosses call me Nibble." },
		{ { "nibble" }, "Not funny! Me full name Golozo Taku Narkat Kash Bartak Har-Alhad, ignorant hu-man!" },
		{ { "golozo taku narkat kash bartak har-alhad" }, "You mispronounce badly, hu-man! But no matter." },
		{ { "time" }, "Eating time for ogre bosses. Cleaning pigsty time foor poor goblin, always and again." },
		{ { "goblins" }, { "Chosen folk of Frog God. Lived free in free goblin city! Golden age of goblins before ogre came! ...", "Now slaves of ogres, mining for crystals. Source of deep shame. You not understand, you no goblin." } },
		{ { "frog god" }, "You not worthy of croaking his name! He no listen to you, he no turn golden eye on you, hu-man!" },
		{ { "hopgoblin" }, { "Him great philosopher goblin, wisest of all! Him see what need be done in thought and deed, and him do it, even if weak minds often not understand. ...", "Him said, goblin need many thoughts, many voices. Him said, freedom in spirit. Him said, responsibility in action. In the end, him make ultimate sacrifice. Said need of many goblins outweigh need of one! But his sad, sad loss." } },
		{ { "swordfish" }, { "Hero of past days, made clever pranks on ogres to save many fellow goblins. Right hand of Sugatrap during trek to find holy mountain, and trusted friend after. ...", "Him patron of secret city. Countless tales of his deeds, told little goblin whelps in their crib! Every goblin want to be like him - feisty, fast and funny Swordfish!" } },
		{ { "sugatrap" }, { "Great forefather. Led goblins to holy mountains to raise city in honour of Frog God. Every goblin whelp know his story! Him lived in dark times. ...", "Then, all under heel of stupid ancient goblin clans, always warring and quarreling with everyone, with orcs, trolls, humans, elves! Not good for goblins! Always hunted above and beneath earth! ...", "But Sugatrap clever! Saw this not way forward to better times. Him thought weapons resort of the stupid. Thought of new things. ...", "Devised traps for flies to offer to Frog God. So God Frog turned golden eyes on him and showed him way. ...", "Sugatrap saw goblins had to leave and build new civilization. But when he tell other goblins, they laugh and say, 'Who you to say we must change goblin ways?' And he say, 'I Am Sugatrap. And I say.' ...", "And they laugh again, and Sugatrap know they never come with him but stay stupid and kill each other. So he killed all who laugh. But he weep to have to kill fellow goblins. ...", "Sad time, long ago now. Rest of goblins clever enough to follow Sugatrap into bright future." } },
		{ { "ogres" }, { "Big, brutes, barbarians. Them worship greed, always greedy. Greedy for crystals! Greedy for tasty food! Greedy for violence! ...", "But goblins will not give up. One day we free again. ...", "And then, will rebuild great city greater than ever, and never be seen again by hulky ogres or hu-mans! Happiness!" } },
		{ { "mines" }, { "Goblin folk use to live happy in secret. Then one day ogre fall into goblin tunnel. Baaaaad day for goblins! ...", "Ogre come and eat goblin babies. Ogre come and make goblin mine for holy crystals. Sacrilege! Slavery! ...", "Ogre take goblin chief as slave in camp. Ignominy! Cannot leave camp! Cannot free people!" } },
		{ { "vuzrog" }, { "Acting chieftain of tribe. Him always hungry, always make me stir horrible ogre soup with goblin bones in it! <sob> ...", "Him see everything as either to be eaten, be beaten or to be used for menial task. Bah." } },
		{ { "mugruu" }, { "Him only ogre in camp with flicker of cleverness. Him learn from hu-man Larek how to trade. Before, him used to make crude tools like rest of ogres. ...", "One time, goblins steal some of Mugruu's tools and ran away. Not know what became of them. Hope they smuggled to people in mines! ...", "But after that, all goblin slaves in camp killed except for me. I left alive as punishment! But will not give up! One day, we goblins free again!" } },
		{ { "ghorza" }, "Ogress of power. Serve horrible hungry god, but she at least not interested in goblins, she always leave Nibble alone." },
		{ { "larek" }, "Him slave like me, baking cookies for glutton chieftain. Him never leave camp again alive." },
	},
	["An Imprisoned Goblin"] = {
		{ { "name" }, "Name lost in sorrow! Took new one to show tragic fate of goblinkind! Garamor Avolok Tor-Mazak!" },
		{ { "garamor avolok tor-mazak" }, "Black Veil on Mind, Shadow on Heart, Tears of Blood, Weeping for Thousands Killed by Greed! Near enough translation." },
		{ { "imprisoned" }, "Got sealed in as example to others, without food or water! Me left here to die! But wait for help! Pray to Frog God that it will come!" },
		{ { "goblins" }, { "Once, goblins stupid and greedy like rest of this world! But then, Frog God gave vision to Sugatrap how to progress. Went to holy mountain! Grew goblin civilization! Peace! Plenty! Harmony! ...", "But alas, goblins lost greatness again, devoured by insatiable ogre appetite for goblin flesh." } },
		{ { "swordfish" }, { "Him best friend of Sugatrap. Found city founding stone, and him become protector of city. ...", "Many great deeds defending first goblin generations from hungry ogres poking around in mountains! Long we safe because of him!" } },
		{ { "hopgoblin" }, "Greatest thinker of golden age. 'I think, therefore I goblin!' When ogre found secret tunnel entrance, it Hopgoblin who told famous riddle to make ogre think long enough, saving hundreds of goblins!" },
		{ { "sugatrap" }, "Long time ago, he given vision by Frog God, and founded hidden city of goblins. Free goblins! First among equals he was! But great times long gone. All devastated by greedy ogres." },
		{ { "ogres" }, "Bane of goblins! Maybe sent to punish us? But why? All we know, they greedy, and they enslave and eat goblins. Horrible fate!" },
		{ { "mines" }, "Slavery! Poor goblins dig through hard earth for precious stones and crystals, all for greedy ogres." },
	},
	["A Goblin Exile"] = {
		{ { "job" }, { "Used to be philosopher priest shaman for East Waterwhirl clans! Keeper of sacredness! Truth teller! But this no say anything to you, hu-man. ...", "These days, me exile hermit waiting for new time. Keep things safe and hallow lost artefacts of goblins, for Frog God to look kindly on our last hope! ...", "Frog God leads me to places where find useful stuff needed for salvation of goblinkind. I pray, his golden eyes lead. I find. I hide." } },
		{ { "frog god" }, "Holy, holy, holy. Poor goblin pray to Frog God for new time of peace for goblins!" },
		{ { "peace" }, "Goblins wait for Third Time of Peace. Will be end of world as we know it. Frog God will return to be tadpole, Night Snake will devour skies and die, and earth will be one with water again." },
		{ { "third time of peace" }, "Hopefully, time near when goblinkind free again. Me await sign every day." },
		{ { "night snake" }, "No story to tell in dark times, not here. Might come when called! Suffice it to say that it chases Frog God and hates cool earth and water, no friend of goblins." },
		{ { "name" }, "Used to have one, when still in city. Left it behind. Now, old hermit waiting for goblin redemption I am. Nemmo Tokrok Argkaz Ar-Vanda Ho'Memot." },
		{ { "nemmo tokrok argkaz ar-vanda ho'memot" }, "Not name, more description of what is. Roughly means, The One Who Is No-One, Whose Name Is Buried in Memories of Days Lost Behind Closed Eyes." },
		{ { "goblins" }, "For long time, goblins safe in mountains. Lived and prospered! Sang songs of golden times, passed on knowledge from old to new goblins! Then ogres came." },
		{ { "ogres" }, "Always hungry, always, take, kill, eat, destroy! Must have been spawn spewn out by Night Snake to prey on poor Frog God children." },
		{ { "nibble", "golozo taku narkat kash bartak har-alhad" }, "You seen Golozo Taku Narkat Kash Bartak Har-Alhad! If him still alive, there still hope. Great leader, almost golden fire of Sugatrap in him. Him never give up." },
		{ { "garamor avolok tor-mazak" }, { "Ah, me know him. Young goblin scholar, heart of philosopher. Best pupil he was! ...", "Him rally other goblins in time of need and bear their soul load. Sign of golden eyes looking on him, great deed and burden, oh yes." } },
		{ { "swordfish" }, { "Him best friend of Sugatrap. Bravest goblin scout, master of disguise and fleet-footed! Found city founding stone! Protector of city! ...", "Dressed up as ogre girl to distract hungry ogres from holy food finders! ...", "Sang snarky songs to lure ogres away from wounded Sugatrap, then ran back and carried him to nearest hidden tunnel entrance! ...", "Lots more stories but no time to tell, hu-man!" } },
		{ { "hopgoblin" }, { "Wisest goblin of past times, founded three school of rival philosophies! Very selfless goblin, died for goblinkind! ...", "His riddle stopped ogre killing long enough for goblins to flee back home, collapsing secret tunnels! But Hopgoblin stay behind and angry ogre kill him and break his staff. ...", "His broken staff in my family for hundred generations! Proud heirloom! One day will be made whole when goblins free again!" } },
		{ { "sugatrap" }, "No! You lie! That not true. Golden eyes averted from you!" },
		{ { "grubokk" }, "That name of mine jailer now? I remember other ogre jailer. Bit him into shin before me went into exile. Heheh." },
	},
	["A Runaway Goblin"] = {
		{ { "name" }, "Oh, kind hu-man asks for goblin name! But too dangerous, am sought goblin! Ogres must not know!" },
		{ { "time" }, "Time for hu-man to go away? Yes indeed!" },
		{ { "job" }, "Am, er, purveyor of things! Yes! Bring stuff where needed, discreetly-like! Heheh!" },
		{ { "runaway" }, "Yes! Not stay at ogre camp! Not wait to become tasty goblin soup, oh no! Not want to wipe hairy ogre backside, no no no!" },
		{ { "ogres" }, "Urgh, ogre smell baaad! Like rotten rat cheese and dragon eggs! Terrible day for goblins when ogres found us! Slavery, sadness, sorrow!" },
		{ { "vuzrog" }, "Big gobbler of sweet. Here free tip for you, hu-man. Throw cookie into air to keep him busy while flee! Heheh." },
		{ { "ghorza" }, "Shaman ogre? She no bother. Dancing around cactus tree, not see small goblin, heheh." },
		{ { "larek" }, "Huh, hu-man who not know how to run. Too busy scribbling down things. Now has to make ogre cookies or become one himself!" },
		{ { "nibble" }, "Ahhh! You spoke to Golozo Taku Narkat Kash Bartak Har-Alhad! Him still alive, that good news!" },
